{
  // What ships. `tsconfig.json` includes the tests so `npm run typecheck` and
  // the editor cover them; this one must not, because `files: ["dist"]` in
  // package.json publishes whatever `tsc` emits.
  //
  // 0.1.2 shipped `dist/tests/` — 32 files and 68.8 kB against 24 and 31.0 kB —
  // because the tests moved into this repository while `include` still said
  // `**/*.ts`. Same shape as `docs/` reaching `copy-assets`: a build defined as
  // "everything except" quietly grows when a sibling directory appears.
  //
  // `scripts/sync-version.ts` is the same shape one release later: release-time
  // tooling with no runtime role, which `npm version` runs from *source* through
  // Node's type stripping and never from `dist`. Compiled it is an extra file in
  // the tarball, and one that would be wrong if anyone ran it — its package root
  // is `import.meta.dirname/..`, which from `dist/scripts/` is `dist/`, the very
  // reason `copy-assets.ts` says `"..", ".."`. `copy-assets.js` stays because
  // `npm run build` invokes it from there.
  //
  // Naming it here is only half of keeping it out. `exclude` trims the *entry*
  // set; a file something in the build imports is pulled back in and emitted
  // regardless, CLI side effects included. So the rewrite both this and `init`
  // need lives in `shared/pins.ts`, which ships on purpose, and a test asserts
  // nothing built imports the script.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Off for everything that is emitted. `tsconfig.json` enables it for the
    // release hook, which runs from source under Node's type stripping and has
    // to name `../shared/pins.ts` literally; a file that *ships* writing a `.ts`
    // specifier would emit an import nothing can resolve, so it fails here
    // instead. Also what makes this config legal at all — the option is refused
    // outright when emit is on.
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": false
  },
  "exclude": ["dist", "tests", "vitest.config.ts", "scripts/sync-version.ts"]
}
